### S5b Kefir — imported, Linux baseline measured

**Declaration directly after a label (2026-11-11, base `a41361e`):**
The front end's synthetic declaration packages are now flattened into the
enclosing block.  The package is not a new lexical scope: ARM must not reuse
its stack slots while the variables live, and cleanup must not run early on
any target.  Unchanged Kefir `std_attributes18` passes all four Clang/vcc
combinations on x86 and ARM, both unity and file-by-file build.  The minimal
baseline gives ARM failures for two live volatile locals; a separate cleanup
regression reveals the same scope failure on x86 too.  The new regression and
switch/statement-expression probes pass 36/36 combinations
(Clang/unity/file-by-file x O0/O2/O3 x two targets x two sources).  Own
suites: x86 233/233 with six existing reference exceptions, ARM 238/238 with
one existing xfail; sema run/batch 887/887 on both builds, diagnostics
225/225.  Evidence: `work/arm-computed-goto/`.  No new full Kefir baseline
is claimed.

**Legacy `_ExtInt` (2026-11-11):** the keyword goes through the same parser
and type path as `_BitInt`, with `-Wdeprecated-type` as in Clang.  Unchanged
`extint1` passes all four Clang/vcc combinations on x86-64.  ARM's Clang
reference rejects 310 bits and remains filtered; separately its unchanged
Clang host is run against vcc callee under QEMU.  `bench/vcc-extint.py`
checks type identity, C89/C11/C23 and warning flags, 24 call combinations on
x86 and 20 on ARM up to 120 bits.  ARM 310 bits is checked separately
against Python-generated bytes, not against a nonexistent Clang reference.
Unity and file-by-file builds give the same result.  PP parity:
920/920 before and after, in both per-process and batch runs.  Artifacts:
`work/results/extint-alias/`, `work/results/extint-{before,after}-{cmp,batch}.log`.

**Combined front-end milestone (2026-11-11, base 2dc4ea3):** Three bounded
fixes: the whole sequence of string literals determines the encoding before
decoding (also late `u`/`U`/`L` and hex escapes); quoted `#embed` searches
the working directory after the includer's directory and before
`--embed-dir`; constant-foldable VLA bounds keep evaluated side effects.
Portable runtime tests, diagnostic tests and a new CI oracle for embed search
are included.

Unity and file-by-file builds pass together.  Kernel sema: 887/887 both
per process and batch; full PP parity including host: 920/920 in both
modes.  Both compiler builds: own x86 tests 224 passed + 6 explicit
reference skips; ARM/QEMU 229 passed + 1 existing xfail, no skips;
diagnostics 224/224; embed oracle 40 comparisons across both Linux targets.
Runtime was also run without the result cache for the file-by-file build.

Unchanged Kefir `string_literals1`, `wide_string_literals2`,
`preprocessor_embed7` and `vla1` pass on x86-64 in all four
Clang/vcc combinations with both builds.  On ARM, embed/VLA pass;
Clang rejects the two string cases' assumptions about signed `wchar_t`,
which are reported as `reference-compile-fail`, never as passed.
The portable string regression passes on ARM/QEMU.  This is a
targeted selection, not a green full Kefir suite.  Frozen patch, bundle,
source/binary manifest and run logs: `work/results/frontend-milestone-2dc`.

The official repo is now `https://git.protopopov.lv/kefir.git`, pinned to
`7c59547068eaa0723b4db83d3fb70f448b0f0cb1`; the old sr.ht HEAD contains
only the move notice.  Source/license metadata is in `bench/kefir-source.json`.
`bench/vcc-kefir.py` inventories 1106 end2end directories: 875 runtime pairs
(875 host files, 889 test files) and 231 compiler-internal snapshot directories.
Each runtime pair keeps all companion files, upstream's profile flags,
active host assertions and Linux linking with pthread/atomic/m.
Clang/Clang must first pass the exit status contract; then
Clang/vcc, vcc/Clang and vcc/vcc are run.  No output comparison is invented.

Raw profiles, base flags, final/mapped flags, environment, exact commands,
source tree hash and file hashes are saved.  The snapshot comes from `git archive` of
the right clean pin.  Unknown profile/make/run contracts are explicitly unsupported.
Decimal capability guards must never become empty passing tests; on ARM
x86 guards/intrinsics/inline asm are also separated.  Internal AST/IR/asmgen
snapshots and upstream's copying of expected output are not run as tests.
Clang rejection is filtered separately; signals, timeouts, missing tools
and silent compiler failures are visible failures with exit status 1, even
when other cases pass.
Ten checkout-only rig tests are included in CI.  This is a new failure
baseline, not a green suite or full coverage of Kefir's internal tests.

